Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||11-13-2001||02:02 AM||||got a "high flow" cat installed on my fiero- used to run 2 3/4" pipe with a single/dual modified series 40 flowmaster- car ripped, especially at the top end- now, after having it made smoggable (CA smog) w/ 2 1/2 inch pipe, high flow cat, and flowmaster series 80 (ran over a rock and the 40 died) the car seems anemic. please with the 0-30 improvement, but now i can barely outrun my friends mercury monterey (400 ci 4bbl) when i used to walk all over it... any ideas for how to compensate? have some interesting ideas for a race only exhaust too.. building it right now.. will post pics/info. thanks for any response.||||reg||1
Z||000001||artherd||11-13-2001||04:26 AM||||Ran my Formula with, and withought, a Catalyst.  Found no real difference.<P>Louder sans-cat.  made me smell bad after working on it with motor running.  So I put one back on.<P>Sounds like something else went wrong.  I'd go back to a 40 series (JESUS what kind of rock dod you hit? check cradle for cracks.  heck, check your engine.)<P>Other than sound, it really didn't make any difference.<P>Right now I am planning on going with 2 sets of 'paralell' cats on the northstar car (4 total, two per bank, in paralell  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  and then a pair of quality silencers.<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000002||Formula88||11-13-2001||08:52 AM||||Same here. I've run both with and without a cat and noticed no real difference.  Sounds like the difference you're getting is from the change in muffler and piping.||||reg||1
Z||000003||thomas_l||11-13-2001||09:12 AM||||This really should go in the tech section but...<P>First go over every inch with a mirror if necessary. Look for kinks or flat sections in the plumbing. Maybe you smashed something else besides the muffler???<P>Then check your exhaust back pressure. Either buy a kit that punches a small hole with self tapping fittings/plugs or rig something in the O2 sensor hole (spark plug thread). Under load, backpressure should be no more than 1-2 psi before the cat. Sometimes exhaust pressure will push the EGR valve open making the power loss even worse (usually takes a totally clogged exhaust or weak EGR for this to happen).<P>Good luck!||||reg||10
Z||000004||88CoupeV6||11-13-2001||10:30 AM||||I've had no cat on both of mine and added Rodney's high flow cat. I lie it better. Sounds deeper and no power loss. I also seem to get better gas mileage for some reason.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||7
Z||000005||FieroSTETZ||11-13-2001||11:20 AM||||the muffler was already hanging down low, the shop that put it on welded it to the cradle, and when i swapped engines i had to cut the hangers. i was on my way to the exhaust shop to yell at them for welding it on when i ran over a rock and punched a hole in the muffler. it was strange, didnt hurt anything else. theres no kinks or anything. i think i need to find a way to check the welds they did- i see no reason why a slight change in pipe diameter, and a different muffler should affect my car THAT much||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||11-13-2001||03:17 PM||||damn, I cant believe a reputable shop welded the muffler to frame !! Anyone knows the exhaust has to be free to move when the engine is under torque. Thats why factory mounted it all on springs.Id be raising hell with them to fix it again right this time.||||reg||1
